+    // Android destroys a window's surface when the app leaves the foreground and gives it a new
+    // ANativeWindow when it comes back. When set, swap chains call this in resize() and move to
+    // the window it returns if that changed. It returns the window with a reference of its own
+    // (released by the swap chain), or nullptr while there is none.
+    typedef ANativeWindow *(*AndroidWindowProvider)();
+    void setAndroidWindowProvider(AndroidWindowProvider provider);
